aml is a small event loop and thread pool library for C. It provides a
uniform event loop interface over epoll (Linux) and kqueue (BSD),
timers, and a thread pool. It is a dependency of neatvnc and wayvnc.

This package installs the shared library, headers, and pkg-config file
(aml1.pc), required to build neatvnc and wayvnc.

Requirements (all part of the Slackware base system):
  - meson
  - ninja

SBo dependencies:
  - none
